{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787060613,"nonce":"00EUJ0XVIjiV3AjUIUx+PaZGQL4=","title":"`refire_grace` decides nothing now that a case cannot be reopened, and the tuning copy still promises it does","message":"**What is wrong.** `refire_grace` existed to answer one question: when an alert resolves and fires again\nshortly after, is that the same episode continuing or a new one? Migration `00054` answered it\npermanently — a case is strictly terminal, and a re-fire always opens a new case at the next `seq`. The\nsetting now decides no transition at all. It was left in place because removing a settings key is its own\ncontract change, and `group_close_delay_s` is pinned against it.\n\n**The demonstration.** T8 is deleted from the transition table and `reopen_count`/`reopen_of` are dropped\nby `00054`, so no code path reads the grace to choose between reopening and opening. Meanwhile\n`web/src/features/settings/tuningCopy.ts:352,360` still tells an operator the window \"reopens the existing\ncase\" — a promise about behaviour that no longer exists in the product.\n\n**Why it matters.** A tuning knob that changes nothing is worse than an absent one: an operator who turns\nit up believes they have bought flap tolerance and has bought nothing, and the next agent to read it will\neither wire it to something or spend a session working out that it is inert. The copy is actively false,\nwhich is the part that reaches users.\n\n**Where.** `internal/tuning` (the setting and its bounds) · `web/src/features/settings/tuningCopy.ts:352,360`\n· `docs/adr/0040-*.md` §6 (records the question as undecided) · `docs/design/SPEC.md` (the §B.3 table and\nthe tuning rows) · wherever `group_close_delay_s` is pinned against it.\n\n**Scope.** small\n\n**Done when.**\n1. `refire_grace` is gone from the settings contract, its bounds, its defaults and its prose.\n2. `group_close_delay_s`'s pinning no longer references it, and whatever that pin was protecting is either\n   still protected or explicitly recorded as no longer needing protection.\n3. No operator-visible copy describes a grace window reopening a case.\n4. ADR 0040 §6 is amended from \"undecided\" to the decision and its reason: flap tolerance belongs at case\n   formation (see the case-retention ticket), not at the lifecycle boundary.","files":null}]}